      "side": 1,
      "message": "This is a proposal for an API shape the reduces friction between Blink and Skia for the very hot code path of glyph advances retrieval. Having a write-converter passed in as a callback really helps avoiding moving from 2 temporary 500 glyphs long vector allocations and initilizations on the Blink side, and moving to straight to the passed-in HarfBuzz buffer. Please see bug for details. \n\nI appreciate your feedback - hope something like this works as an extension to the StrikeRef API.",
